        "title": "Multiplying a Matrix With Variable Entries by a Column Vector"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "aa477682-d6c6-50d6-b5d0-d2e4a3852cc1",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "If \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}m & n & -m \\\\ m & -n & -m \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$u=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ l \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $Pu.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Pu=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pu & =\\begin{bmatrix}m & n & -m \\\\ m & -n & -m \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ l \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}m\\cdot 1+n\\cdot l+(-m)\\cdot 1 \\\\ m\\cdot 1+(-n)\\cdot l+(-m)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 0\\cdot 1+2\\cdot l+0\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}m+l\\cdot n-m \\\\ m-l\\cdot n-m \\\\ 0+2l+0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}l\\cdot n \\\\ -l\\cdot n \\\\ 2l\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
